※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4566

※ Whoever holds the reference was promised that nothing else changes the place:
※ a `&mut` that it is alone, a `&` that the place does not change at all.
※ Writing the name would be exactly the change that was promised not to happen,
※ whichever kind of reference is out -- so this is refused where the `&` is
※ shared as much as where a `&mut` is not.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: mut u8 = 1u8
    let only: &u8 = &n
    n ← 2u8
    if only⌖ ≠ 2u8:
        1u6
    else:
        0u6
